update public.blog_posts
set title='How to Plan Online Quran Lessons Across US Time Zones', seo_title='Online Quran Lessons Across US Time Zones | OQC', seo_description='Plan online Quran lessons in US time zones, compare local class times and check daylight saving changes before arranging a recurring class or free trial.', excerpt='Plan online Quran lessons in US time zones, compare local class times and check daylight saving changes before arranging a recurring class or free trial.', seo_focus_keyword='online Quran lessons US time zones', body_html=$article$
<p>To arrange online Quran lessons in the USA, send the coordinator your city, preferred date and local time. A 5:00 p.m. lesson in New York is at 2:00 p.m. in Los Angeles. Giving the city and date helps the coordinator account for seasonal clock changes before confirming a weekly slot.</p>
<h2>How do the six US time zones affect Quran class times?</h2>
<p>The 50 states use six principal zones: Eastern, Central, Mountain, Pacific, Alaska and Hawaii–Aleutian. Here is the same appointment on a winter and summer date under current rules.</p>
<table><thead><tr><th>City</th><th>January 15, 2027</th><th>July 15, 2027</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>New York</td><td>5:00 p.m.</td><td>5:00 p.m.</td></tr><tr><td>Chicago</td><td>4:00 p.m.</td><td>4:00 p.m.</td></tr><tr><td>Denver</td><td>3:00 p.m.</td><td>3:00 p.m.</td></tr><tr><td>Los Angeles</td><td>2:00 p.m.</td><td>2:00 p.m.</td></tr><tr><td>Phoenix</td><td>3:00 p.m.</td><td>2:00 p.m.</td></tr><tr><td>Anchorage</td><td>1:00 p.m.</td><td>1:00 p.m.</td></tr><tr><td>Honolulu</td><td>12:00 p.m.</td><td>11:00 a.m.</td></tr></tbody></table>
<p>Use the <a href="/locations/united-states">Online Quran Classes USA scheduling guide</a> for your own city and date. The <a href="https://www.transportation.gov/regulations/time-act">US Department of Transportation’s Uniform Time guide</a> explains official zone boundaries.</p>
<h2>When do US clocks change in 2027?</h2>
<p>Under current rules, participating areas move clocks forward on March 14, 2027, and back on November 7, 2027. Hawaii and most of Arizona keep standard time year-round. The Navajo Nation observes daylight saving time. Phoenix and Denver share the same clock during winter, and Denver runs one hour ahead of Phoenix during daylight saving time. Check the <a href="https://www.nist.gov/pml/time-and-frequency-division/popular-links/daylight-saving-time-dst">NIST daylight saving rules and exceptions</a>.</p>
<p>Ask which local time the recurring booking follows. If you want 5:00 p.m. in your city every Tuesday, ask the coordinator to check a Tuesday before and after the clock change and confirm what the calendar invitation shows.</p>
<figure><img src="/images/learning/usa-online-quran-learning-r2-800.webp" alt="Parent and child using a laptop for Quran study at home" loading="lazy"><figcaption>Share two local-time windows that fit your household’s weekly routine.</figcaption></figure>
<h2>How can you fit lessons around school, work and siblings?</h2>
<p>Give one preferred weekday window and one alternative. Leave time for school pickup, homework or a shift change. If siblings need separate lessons, ask about consecutive slots and see the <a href="/blog/family-quran-learning-multiple-children">guide to planning Quran lessons for siblings</a>.</p>
<h2>What should you confirm about the course, teacher and fee?</h2>
<p>Share the learner’s level and goals. New readers can explore <a href="/courses/noorani-qaida">Noorani Qaida</a>, while learners who already read can explore <a href="/courses/quran-nazara">Quran reading with Tajweed</a>. Online Quran College offers live one-to-one lessons. You can request a male or female teacher and a preferred teaching language. The coordinator will confirm availability and can discuss how a parent may observe a lesson.</p>
<p>Confirm the lesson length, weekly frequency, rescheduling terms and billing currency. Review the <a href="/pricing?currency=USD">published USD packages</a> and the <a href="/blog/online-quran-class-fees-usa-comparison">US Quran class fee comparison</a>.</p>
<h2>What should you include in a US trial request?</h2>
<ul><li>Your city and state, a preferred date and two local-time options.</li><li>The learner’s reading level, course interest and teacher or language preference.</li><li>An email address you check and, if using a US WhatsApp number, the +1 country code.</li></ul>
<p><a href="/free-trial?country=United%20States&amp;currency=USD">Request a three-day Quran class trial</a>. The trial is available on eligible plans without a credit card. The Weekend plan is excluded.</p>
$article$, reading_minutes=4, seo_noindex=false, version=version+1, updated_at=now()
